  "courseName": "Introductory Molecular Biology (200-level)",
  "estimatedLength": "35 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the structural components of DNA, including the sugar-phosphate backbone, nitrogenous bases, and hydrogen bonds that stabilize base pairing.",
    "Apply complementary base-pairing rules to infer DNA sequences and explain the chemical basis for A-T and G-C pairing.",
    "Describe antiparallel strand orientation and connect 5' to 3' directionality to DNA structure and replication.",
    "Trace the roles of helicase, single-strand binding proteins, DNA polymerase, and DNA ligase at the replication fork.",
    "Explain why leading and lagging strands are synthesized differently and how Okazaki fragments arise.",
    "Define semiconservative replication and predict the composition of daughter DNA molecules after successive rounds of replication."
